# Cloudberry's PAX tests (contrib/pax_storage/pax_schedule), as the port runs
# them on a coordinator and three segments, in the schedule's order and
# groups.
#
#   run   the test runs here; cloudberry/ holds a difference reviewed and
#         kept, where it has one.  A third word names the group it runs in,
#         "main" when there is none, "*" for every group: each group is a job
#         of its own on a cluster of its own (../jobs, PAX_GROUP), in the
#         schedule's order and groups -- toast, whose 100 MB values take two
#         minutes, beside the rest, and the setup and the teardown in each
#   skip  it needs what the port does not have: the rest of the line says
#         what
run  setup      *
run  pax_inject_fault
skip cbdb_parallel  intra-segment parallelism, which the port has not before M7 (decision 2): gp.enable_parallel is accepted and a segment runs a slice in one process
run  alter_distributed
run  toast      toast
run  toast_failed
run  detoast
run  ddl
run  numeric
run  types
run  filter
run  update
run  statistics_bloom_filter
run  delete_bloom_stats
run  filter_tree
run  filter_tree_arithmetic
run  filter_tree_root_quals
run  statistics/statistics
run  delete_sum_stats
run  statistics/min_max_time_types
run  statistics/min_max_text_types
run  statistics/min_max_other_types
run  statistics/min_max_net_types
run  statistics/min_max_int_types
run  statistics/min_max_geo_types
run  statistics/min_max_float_types
run  statistics/min_max_bit_byte_types
run  visimap_vec_compact
run  visimap_vec_storage
run  default_value
run  dictionary_encoding
run  cluster
run  db_size_functions
run  teardown   *
